      <h1 class="about-title">About Culinary Judge</h1>

      <p class="about-text">
        Culinary Judge is a web application designed to manage culinary
        competitions and simplify the judging process. It allows an
        administrator to manage judges, competitors, scoring groups,
        and evaluation criteria in one place.
      </p>

      <p class="about-text">
        The administrator can create accounts for judges, add competitors
        and their school information, and define scoring groups such as
        appetizers, main courses, and desserts. Each group can contain
        multiple evaluation criteria, such as taste, presentation, and
        temperature, with predefined minimum and maximum points.
      </p>

      <p class="about-text">
        Judges log in using accounts created by the administrator.
        They can view competitors, review the scoring criteria, and
        assign points according to the competition rules.
      </p>

      <p class="about-text">
        The application stores scores for each judge, competitor, and
        criterion. It calculates total scores and displays a leaderboard
        ranking competitors by their results.
      </p>

      <p class="about-text">
        Culinary Judge aims to make culinary competitions more organized,
        transparent, and efficient by providing a centralized system for
        managing participants, evaluating dishes, and reviewing
        competition results.
      </p>

      <p class="about-text">
        <strong>Technologies:</strong> Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB,
        Mongoose, EJS, JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.
      </p>

